        {
          "id": 2930462721,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "It can (although modern OSes use a slab allocator so I don't know the effect.) On the other hand, MAX_ITEM_LEN is 8192, which is probably way too much to allocate for `linenum_buf` for the typical case.\n\nMaybe a better solution is a GString (/wmem_strbuf with NULL allocator) and calling set_size which doesn't free the memory, but will expand it as needed.",
