      ],
      "title": "mate: Try to prevent a bogus gcc format-truncation warning",
      "message": "mate: Try to prevent a bogus gcc format-truncation warning\n\nGLib g_malloc terminates the program on memory allocation failure\nhttps://docs.gtk.org/glib/func.malloc.html\nand so never returns NULL. Sometimes gcc when optimizing and using\nFORTIFY_SOURCE doesn't seem to notice that, e.g. in this Ubuntu\nbuild log:\nhttps://launchpadlibrarian.net/834957085/buildlog_ubuntu-plucky-amd64.wireshark_4.7.0-0~202512020016~ubuntu25.04.1_BUILDING.txt.gz\n\n(Also see commit c02d0066b5e16d575f5a606b84246fd8b0349d6e for a similar\ncase in the capture library).\n\nUse a GString and g_string_append_printf (and resizing it back to zero)\ninstead of g_malloc'ing a big buffer at the start to repeatedly snprintf\ninto in the hopes of confusing gcc less. This will only allocate space\nas necessary instead of always allocating 8192 bytes (which is almost\nsurely more than needed.)\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-12-03T06:27:34.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
